course: dictionary
lesson: 10847
title: Up and down: the word vertically
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vertically is an adverb, so it tells you how something moves or stands. It means in an up-and-down direction, straight up, at a right angle to the ground. A flagpole stands vertically, and a rocket launched straight up goes vertically.
explain: In maths, vertical lines go up and down, like the edge of a door. A line that goes from side to side is horizontal, so vertically and horizontally are a pair of directions. When you read a column of numbers from top to bottom, you read it vertically.
explain: People sometimes use words in playful ways. «"Vertically challenged" is a joking way to say short.» It is a joke, so use the plain meaning, up and down, when you work in maths or science.
fact: Vertically means in an up-and-down direction, straight up or at a right angle to the ground.
fact: Vertical lines go up and down; horizontal lines go from side to side.
fact: In a graph, the y-axis runs vertically.
fact: A shape can be flipped vertically, which means it is reflected up and down.
fact: «Vertically and horizontally» means in both directions: up and down, and side to side.
exercise: «The rocket was launched vertically into the sky.» What does vertically mean here? | Sideways, along the ground | Slowly and quietly | Round and round in a circle | *Straight up, at a right angle to the ground
exercise: In a graph, which axis runs vertically? | The horizontal line along the bottom | The x-axis | The title of the graph | *The y-axis
exercise: Which line goes vertically? | A line along the bottom of a page | *A line from the ceiling down to the floor | A line across the middle of a table | A line that goes round in a circle
test: «Vertically challenged» is a joking way to say what? | Clever | Loud | Tall | *Short
test: Which word is the partner of vertically in the phrase «vertically and horizontally»? | Quietly | Slowly | Backwards | *Horizontally
exam: When you read a column of numbers from top to bottom, you read it | Backwards | Diagonally | *Vertically | Horizontally
